A recommendation is a category-A-recommendation and is an evidence-type-4-recommendation.
Every clinician should evaluate an opioid-benefit with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a therapy-start for a subacute-pain and should evaluate an opioid-risk with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a therapy-start for a subacute-pain.
Every clinician should evaluate an opioid-benefit with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a therapy-start for a chronic-pain and should evaluate an opioid-risk with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a therapy-start for a chronic-pain.
Every clinician should evaluate an opioid-benefit with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a dosage-escalation and should evaluate an opioid-risk with a patient after 1 week before 4 weeks after a dosage-escalation.
Every clinician should reevaluate an opioid-benefit with a patient during a regular-follow-up and should reevaluate an opioid-risk with a patient during a regular-follow-up.
